Manual: {
	Title: Cultivator's Manual
	Received: You received the Cultivator's Manual. Use it to learn about the Xianxia world
	Previous: Previous
	Next: Next
	Close: Close
	IndexButton: Index
	PageNumber: Page {0}/{1}
	ScrollForMore: Scroll for more
	AlchemyRequirement: Alchemy: {0}, {1} Stage

	RecipeSections: {
		NoviceAttire: Novice Disciple Attire
		MaterialsEquipment: Materials, Equipment and Weapons
		FormationCores: Permanent Formation Cores
		AccessoriesTechniques: Accessories, Techniques and Basic Pills
		CauldronsBeastPills: Cauldrons, Compasses and Spirit Beast Pills
		ProgressionPills: Cultivation Progression Pills
		UtilityPills: Utility Pills
	}

	Index: {
		Title: Index
		Hint: Select a section to open it directly

		Entries: {
			Fundamentals: Cultivation Fundamentals
			QiMeditation: Qi, QiEXP and Meditation
			PassiveAbilities: Passive Abilities
			CombatTechniques: Combat Techniques
			Movement: Movement and Ability Wheel
			BreakthroughResources: Breakthroughs and Resources
			WorldConfiguration: World Configuration
			CraftingRecipes: Crafting Recipes
			CultivationGrowth: Stat Growth
			QiRequirements: Qi and QiEXP Requirements
			SpiritualQiZones: Spiritual Qi Zones
			SpiritMines: Spirit Stone Mines
			AbilityProgression: Ability Tree and Levels
			SpiritBeasts: Spirit Beasts
			AlchemyPath: Alchemy Path
			SectSystem: Sects and Missions
			FormationPath: Permanent Formations
			AdvancedPills: Advanced Pill Recipes
		}
	}

	Pages: {
		Page0: {
			Title: Cultivation Fundamentals
			Body:
				'''
				Cultivation is divided into five Realms: Mortal, Qi Gathering, Foundation Establishment, Core Formation and Nascent Soul.

				Each Realm contains 9 Stages. Every advancement increases health, defense, damage, speed and other statistics. Later Stages require progressively more QiEXP.

				The upper bar displays current Qi and QiEXP. Qi powers techniques and defenses; QiEXP represents permanent progress and does not decrease when an ability is used. Hover over the bar to inspect the next advancement, its stat bonuses, future abilities and Tribulation preparation estimate.

				The /cultivation command displays your current Realm, Stage, bonuses and recovery rates.
				'''
		}

		Page1: {
			Title: Qi, QiEXP and Meditation
			Body:
				'''
				Qi is your usable reserve. QiEXP is permanent experience required to advance. Spending Qi never causes the loss of a Stage or Realm.

				While Qi is below QiEXP, passive recovery scales by Realm: 1 / 2 / 4 / 8 / 16 Qi per second.

				Press [{0}] once while remaining still to begin meditating, then press it again to stop. Toggle meditation is enabled by default and can be changed to hold mode in the client configuration. Moving, attacking, mounting, opening chat or opening the Cultivation Menu stops meditation. If Qi is missing, meditation restores it at 10x speed. If the reserve fills partway through a meditation second, the remaining time immediately cultivates new QiEXP; upkeep from toggle abilities therefore does not block progression. Base growth is 1 / 4 / 16 / 64 / 256 QiEXP per second depending on Realm.

				You can meditate while flying if you remain still. Pendants, talismans, armor and pills can improve these rates.
				'''
		}

		Page2: {
			Title: Passive Abilities
			Body:
				'''
				SPIRITUAL BREATHING - Mortal
				Always active. Increases passive Qi recovery by 10% and trains while restoring missing Qi.

				QI SENSE - Qi Gathering
				Reveals creatures, treasure and danger. Costs 1 Qi/s. Toggle it from the Ability Wheel or with /qisense on|off.

				QI PROTECTION - Foundation Establishment
				Absorbs incoming damage at a cost of 5 Qi per damage, including damage over time from fire, poison and similar debuffs. When breath is exhausted underwater, it also spends Qi to prevent drowning while keeping the breath meter at its last sliver. Cultivation life regeneration is applied before the shield and can reduce or overcome negative regeneration. A spiritual shield appears when activated. Toggle it from the wheel or with /qiprotection on|off.

				GOLDEN CORE CIRCULATION - Core Formation
				Always active. Reduces Qi consumed by abilities by 5% and trains whenever you spend Qi.

				NASCENT SOUL REGENERATION - Nascent Soul
				Always active. Grants +4 life regeneration and trains while healing wounds.
				'''
		}

		Page3: {
			Title: Combat Techniques
			Body:
				'''
				QI RESISTANCE [{0}] - Qi Gathering
				Consumes 60 Qi and grants +10 defense for 1 minute.

				FIREBALL [{1}] - Qi Gathering
				Launches a fiery sphere. Damage, cost and size scale together. The explosion can break terrain.

				QI PALM [{2}] - Qi Gathering
				Projects a large spiritual palm with strong knockback. Damage, size and cost increase with cultivation, and it can destroy terrain. It can also be used through the Qi Palm Technique item.

				SPIRITUAL PRESSURE [{3}] - Nascent Soul
				Toggles an aura that consumes 25 Qi/s, periodically damages and slows enemies. Radius and damage increase with Stage; bosses resist more of the slowing effect. Its compact visual rings do not represent the full damage radius.

				NIGHT VISION [{4}] - Foundation Establishment
				Toggle enhanced vision and a spiritual light aura around your character, allowing exploration in complete darkness without illuminating the entire screen. The aura radius grows with mastery. It costs 3 Qi per second at level 1, 2 Qi per second from level 8 and 1 Qi per second from level 15.
				'''
		}

		Page4: {
			Title: Movement and Ability Wheel
			Body:
				'''
				FLAME STEP [{0}] - Foundation Establishment
				Dash in the direction of the movement keys or cursor, damaging enemies and igniting the path.

				QI FLIGHT [{1}] - Core Formation
				Toggle flight on or off. It consumes 1 Qi/s and becomes faster with every Realm. You can meditate while hovering motionless. Opening the Ability Menu or chat holds you stationary in the air while the normal Qi cost continues, so writing commands never disables flight.

				VOID STEP [{2}] - Nascent Soul
				Teleport to the cursor. It also works on the fullscreen map. Costs 20 Qi + 2 Qi per 2 blocks traveled and finds a clear space near the selected point.

				ABILITY WHEEL [{3}]
				Hold the key to view abilities, requirements, controls and passive states. Click a passive to toggle it.
				'''
		}

		Page5: {
			Title: Breakthroughs, Resources and Alchemy
			Body:
				'''
				Reaching the QiEXP threshold causes a breakthrough. From Core Formation onward, you must confirm and survive a Heavenly Tribulation. Cancelling only postpones the attempt and never removes QiEXP; meditate again with full Qi to reopen the confirmation. Failing the actual Tribulation still removes the failed breakthrough progress. The first contains 9 lightning strikes.

				Heavenly lightning pierces ordinary defenses. At base mastery, Qi Protection consumes about 12% of maximum Qi per Core Formation strike and blocks 70% of its health damage; the rest penetrates the shield. Nascent Soul strikes consume about 15% and deal substantially more damage. Qi Protection mastery lowers the reserve cost. Arrive with full Qi, healing and suitable equipment.

				Spirit Stones cannot be crafted: they are mined from Spirit Crystal veins. Spirit Jade and Profound Iron make bars for armor, accessories, weapons and Flying Swords.

				The Alchemy Cauldron crafts pills. A Qi Recovery Pill restores 100 Qi without increasing QiEXP; other pills temporarily improve meditation, defense and damage.

				The Flying Sword requires Qi Gathering and consumes Qi with every launch. It automatically homes in on the closest visible enemy within 60 blocks; if no target is found it continues normally, then returns to its owner.
				'''
		}

		Page6: {
			Title: World Configuration
			Body:
				'''
				In the mod's Config menu, the ABILITY WORLD DESTRUCTION section controls which techniques may break terrain.

				The master switch disables all ability destruction at once. Below it, Fireball, Qi Palm and Flame Step can be configured separately.

				Every option is enabled by default. These are server settings, so multiplayer uses the host or server choices.

				CLIENT INTERFACE AND EFFECTS
				Each player can move and scale the Qi bar, hide the Qi Concentration line and reduce Xianxia particles, spiritual lights, auras and trails. These client settings never alter damage or server gameplay.

				DEBUG COMMANDS
				Use /xiadebug help to list progression, Qi, ability, effect, Tribulation and Sect testing tools. Use /xiadebug sect max to set the Verdant Cloud Sect rank to maximum. Debug commands work immediately in single-player. In multiplayer they are disabled by default and must be enabled by the server; when enabled, every player can use them, so keep them off on public servers.
				'''
		}

		Recipes1: {
			Title: Complete Crafting Catalogue
			Body:
				'''
				MATERIALS AND STATIONS
				Spirit Jade Bar: 4 Spirit Jade Ore - Furnace
				Profound Iron Bar: 4 Profound Iron Ore - Hellforge
				Alchemy Cauldron: 10 Profound Iron Bars + 5 Spirit Jade Bars + 3 Spirit Stones - Anvil

				SPIRIT JADE ARMOR - ANVIL
				Headpiece: 10 Spirit Jade Bars + 1 Spirit Stone
				Robe: 18 Spirit Jade Bars + 2 Spirit Stones
				Leggings: 14 Spirit Jade Bars + 1 Spirit Stone

				WEAPONS - ANVIL
				Spirit Jade Sword: 8 Spirit Jade Bars
				Profound Iron Spear: 10 Profound Iron Bars + 2 Spirit Stones
				Flying Sword: 12 Spirit Jade Bars + 3 Spirit Stones
				'''
		}

		Recipes2: {
			Title: Recipes - Accessories, Techniques and Pills
			Body:
				'''
				ACCESSORIES
				Profound Iron Ring: 6 Profound Iron Bars + 2 Spirit Stones - Anvil
				Spirit Jade Pendant: 6 Spirit Jade Bars + 2 Spirit Stones - Anvil
				Spirit Gathering Talisman: 5 Silk + 3 Spirit Jade Bars + 3 Spirit Stones - Work Bench

				TECHNIQUES AND GUIDES
				Fireball Technique: Book + Spirit Stone + 5 Fallen Stars - Bookcase
				Qi Palm Technique: Book + 2 Spirit Stones + 5 Fallen Stars - Bookcase
				Spirit Vein Compass: Compass + 8 Gold or Platinum Bars + 5 Fallen Stars + 3 Amethysts - Anvil
				Cultivator's Manual: Book + Spirit Stone - Work Bench

				PILLS x2 - ALCHEMY CAULDRON
				Qi Recovery: Bottled Water + 2 Daybloom + Moonglow + Spirit Stone
				Spirit Gathering: Bottled Water + 2 Moonglow + Waterleaf + 3 Spirit Jade Ore + Spirit Stone
				Body Tempering: Bottled Water + 2 Blinkroot + Deathweed + 3 Profound Iron Ore + Spirit Stone
				'''
		}

		CultivationGrowth: {
			Title: Stage and Realm Growth
			Body:
				'''
				Bonuses are cumulative and increase rapidly in higher Realms. Entering Stage 1 of a new Realm grants 3 times that Realm's normal Stage increase.

				INCREASE PER STAGE
				Mortal: +3 life, +0.5 defense, +0.5% damage
				Qi Gathering: +8 life, +1 defense, +1.5% damage
				Foundation Establishment: +20 life, +2 defense, +4% damage
				Core Formation: +50 life, +5 defense, +9% damage
				Nascent Soul: +120 life, +12 defense, +20% damage

				Each increase also grants movement speed, critical chance, damage reduction and life regeneration. These secondary bonuses follow the same Realm-based growth.
				'''
		}

		QiRequirements: {
			Title: Qi and QiEXP Requirements
			Body:
				'''
				To advance, fill your reserve to the new QiEXP threshold. The cost increases with every Stage and makes a large jump upon entering a higher Realm.

				COST OF EACH STAGE
				Mortal: 25 to 130 QiEXP
				Qi Gathering: 300 to 1,100 QiEXP
				Foundation Establishment: 1,500 to 5,500 QiEXP
				Core Formation: 7,500 to 27,500 QiEXP
				Nascent Soul: 37,500 to 137,500 QiEXP

				The listed cost is added to the total threshold already reached. Usable Qi and QiEXP remain separate: spending Qi on abilities never reduces permanent progress.
				'''
		}

		SpiritualQiZones: {
			Title: High Spiritual Qi Zones
			Body:
				'''
				Spirit Stone mines radiate Qi into the surrounding area. Meditating or passively recovering Qi near a mine grants a multiplier shown below the Qi bar.

				CONCENTRATION WITHIN 60 BLOCKS
				Level 0 - no crystals: +0%
				Level 1 - 1 to 50 crystals: +100% (2x total)
				Level 2 - 51 to 100 crystals: +200% (3x total)
				Levels 3-9 - every 50 additional crystals grant another +100%
				Level 10 - at least 451 crystals: +1000% (11x total)

				The multiplier affects both meditation and passive Qi recovery. The current level, including Level 0, is always displayed below the Qi bar. The radius and the entire mechanic can be changed in the server configuration. Mining the crystals lowers the concentration and may remove the zone completely.
				'''
		}

		SpiritMines: {
			Title: Spirit Stone Mines
			Body:
				'''
				Mines are natural chambers in the Cavern layer. A continuous shell of Spirit Crystal surrounds the chamber and more crystals emerge from its floor.

				SIZES
				Small: about 16-24 blocks wide
				Medium: about 28-40 blocks wide
				Large: about 44-60 blocks wide

				Every world contains at least one mine of each size. Small mines are common, medium mines less frequent and large mines rare.

				The Spirit Vein Compass locates the nearest vein, then shows its direction and distance for 10 seconds. Its default search radius is 250 blocks and is configurable by the server.

				Mines are created only during world generation. Spirit Stones are finite and do not regenerate automatically.
				'''
		}

		Recipes3: {
			Title: Compass Upgrades and Beast Alchemy
			Body: Higher compass versions increase detection range. Spirit Beast materials can be refined into powerful pills at the Alchemy Cauldron.
		}

		Recipes4: {
			Title: Realm Progression Pills
			Body: Advanced pills complete the High Stage of each Tier and the Nascent Soul progression.
		}

		Recipes5: {
			Title: Utility Pill Recipes
			Body: Specialized pills prepare Tribulations, attract Spirit Beasts or conceal the cultivator.
		}

		AbilityProgression: {
			Title: Ability Tree and Mastery
			Body:
				'''
				Open the ability list with [{0}]. Techniques are divided into Realm rows, and each card shows its icon, name, active or passive type, level and EXP bar. Passives are shown before active abilities in every row. Available abilities are illuminated, while abilities from future Realms remain visible but locked.

				Each ability earns EXP when used successfully. Meditation, Flight, Qi Sense and Spiritual Pressure progress during continuous use. Offensive techniques earn EXP on successful casts, and Qi Protection progresses when it absorbs damage.

				The maximum level is 20. Leveling improves power, duration, consumption, speed or cooldown according to the ability. Required EXP grows quadratically.

				The Paths tab is located at the top of the same menu. It contains cultivator professions and is ready for more to be added. The Alchemy Path is currently available, showing the Alchemy Cauldron and known pills.
				'''
		}

		SpiritBeasts: {
			Title: Spirit Beasts
			Body:
				'''
				Spirit Beasts cultivate the same Realms as players. Their nameplate shows Realm, Stage and relative danger. A beast one Realm above you can be a lethal encounter, so inspect the label before attacking.

				KNOWN BEASTS
				Spirit Hare - Mortal - daytime surface, including forest, snow, jungle and beach. Timid and usually flees.
				Jade Horn Deer - Qi Gathering - daytime surface, including forest, snow, jungle and beach. Charges when threatened.
				Flame-Tailed Fox - Foundation Establishment - surface at night, including forest, snow, jungle and beach. Dashes and launches spiritual flame.
				Thunderclaw Tiger - Core Formation - jungle surface at night. An elite beast using leaps and lightning.
				The Dungeon and Desert do not currently host Spirit Beasts.

				DISTANCE FROM WORLD SPAWN
				0+ blocks: Spirit Hare
				200+ blocks: Jade Horn Deer
				450+ blocks: Flame-Tailed Fox
				700+ blocks: Thunderclaw Tiger
				The average Stage rises continuously until reaching maximum strength at about 1,200 blocks. This uses the shared world spawn, not personal beds, and therefore remains consistent in multiplayer.

				Beasts also begin appearing when your cultivation approaches their Realm. Their life, damage, defense and rewards scale with Stage. Relative danger compares both Realm and Stage. They drop fur, blood, elemental essences and Realm Beast Cores used for new pills.

				Natural spawning and its rate can be changed in the server configuration. Use /xiadebug spawncheck to diagnose the current area or /xiadebug beast <hare|deer|fox|tiger> to summon one in single-player.
				'''
		}

		AlchemyPath: {
			Title: The Alchemist's Path
			Body:
				'''
				Alchemy has five cultivation Tiers, and every Tier contains Low, Middle and High Stages. Crafting any Xianxia pill at an Alchemy Cauldron grants Path EXP. Reaching the required Tier and Stage unlocks stronger recipes. Every advancement improves the chance of producing one additional pill and reduces the chance of separating Pill Dregs.

				ALCHEMY TIERS
				Tier 0 - Mortal - Low, Middle, High
				Tier 1 - Qi Gathering - Low, Middle, High
				Tier 2 - Foundation Establishment - Low, Middle, High
				Tier 3 - Core Formation - Low, Middle, High
				Tier 4 - Nascent Soul - Low, Middle, High
				After completing High Stage, the Path advances to Low Stage of the next Tier. Tier 4 High is the current maximum.

				SPIRITUAL HERBS
				Spirit Grass seeds can emerge from ordinary vegetation. Fire Lotus seeds are associated with deserts, Moon Dew Flower seeds with jungles, and Ironroot seeds with snow biomes. These drops work in existing worlds. Plant seeds on suitable solid ground, allow them to pass through three growth stages, then harvest and replant them.

				CAULDRON GRADES
				Alchemy Cauldron - basic refinement.
				Spirit Jade Cauldron - +5% bonus yield and -7% impurity chance.
				Profound Alchemy Cauldron - +10% bonus yield and -14% impurity chance.
				Upgraded Cauldrons also satisfy recipes requiring the basic Alchemy Cauldron.

				PILL QUALITY
				Every refined pill receives a persistent quality: Impure, Common, Refined, Earth Grade or Heaven Grade. Quality is rolled when the recipe is completed and is shared by every pill in that crafted stack. Pills of different qualities cannot merge into the same stack.
				Impure - 70% effect, 135% saturation.
				Common - 100% effect, 100% saturation.
				Refined - 115% effect, 90% saturation.
				Earth Grade - 135% effect, 75% saturation.
				Heaven Grade - 160% effect, 60% saturation.
				Alchemy mastery above the recipe requirement and improved Cauldrons raise the quality roll. The impurity chance can instead force an Impure result and produce Pill Dregs. Quality scales instant restoration, cleansing power and buff duration; the tooltip displays the exact modified saturation cost.

				PILL SATURATION
				Every consumed pill adds saturation. As saturation rises, pill effectiveness falls gradually to 50%. A pill cannot be consumed if it would exceed 100 saturation. Saturation naturally decreases over time, preventing unlimited pill stacking while preserving their strategic use.

				Open the cultivation menu and select Paths > Alchemy to inspect Tier, Stage, EXP, current saturation, pill effectiveness and refinement bonuses. The Alchemy page is divided into five Tier rows; every pill appears beside its Realm Tier with the Low, Middle or High Stage required to unlock it. For testing, use /xiadebug alchemy <tier 0-4> <low|middle|high> or /xiadebug alchemy saturation <0-100>.
				'''
		}

		SectSystem: {
			Title: Verdant Cloud Sect
			Body:
				'''
				The Sect Elder can move into an available house, but accepts disciples only after they reach Qi Gathering. Speak with Elder Jian to enter the Verdant Cloud Sect and receive your first Contribution Tokens.

				SECT RANKS
				Outer Disciple - granted on joining.
				Inner Disciple - 100 lifetime contribution.
				Core Disciple - 300 lifetime contribution.
				Sect Elder - 750 lifetime contribution.
				Contribution Tokens are a separate currency spent in the Sect Shop. Lifetime contribution is never lost when tokens are spent.

				MISSIONS
				The Elder assigns Realm-scaled missions involving Spirit Beasts, Spirit Stones, pill refinement, Spirit Vein exploration and Heavenly Tribulations. Complete the objective, return to the Elder and claim Contribution Tokens. A short waiting period follows each completed assignment.

				SECT TECHNIQUES
				Sword Intent - Outer Disciple passive. Improves Flying Sword damage and gains mastery when a Flying Sword hits.
				Spirit Sword Rain [{0}] - Inner Disciple active technique. Fires five spiritual swords directly from the cultivator toward the cursor. Their maximum range reaches the cursor, but never falls below the normal Flying Sword range. They home onto enemies inside that range; damage and efficiency rise with mastery.
				Sect Protection Formation [{1}] - Core Disciple active technique. Deploys a rotating ritual array beneath a large three-dimensional turquoise protective dome. A nearby Spirit Stone vein powers and repairs it automatically. Otherwise it uses donated reserve, then 1-3 of the owner's Qi each second; if neither is available, it consumes one Spirit Stone from the owner's inventory and stores 250 Qi. It repels nearby enemies and uses its own integrity before Qi Protection. Other cultivators receive defensive bonuses while inside; if they meditate there, they voluntarily donate 1-4 Qi per second. Donated Qi repairs 30 integrity each, enters the upkeep reserve and temporarily increases maximum integrity and formation size by 25% per supporter, up to four supporters. Press the technique key again to dismiss it.

				Open Cultivation Menu > Sect to inspect rank progress, current tokens, mission progress and learned techniques. Technique manuals and spiritual supplies are purchased from the Sect Elder.
				'''
		}

		FormationPath: {
			Title: Permanent Formations
			Body:
				'''
				ARRAY FORMATIONS PATH
				Open Cultivation Menu > Paths > Array Formations to inspect its Tier, Stage, EXP and current trial. Spirit Stones used as fuel never grant Path EXP. Formation mastery is earned by maintaining an array during real combat, absorbing damage, connecting a new Spirit Vein and intercepting Heavenly Tribulation lightning. Path mastery unlocks the structural ranks that a Core may reach, but no longer upgrades any structure automatically.

				Each Stage requires both enough EXP and a practical trial. Low Stage tests sustained combat operation, Middle Stage tests cumulative damage absorption, and High Stage requires a special achievement. Tier 0 requires a Spirit Vein link, Tier 1 requires advanced defensive experience, and later Tiers require increasingly many Tribulation strikes. Advancing to the next Tier also requires reaching its corresponding cultivation Realm.

				PERMANENT FORMATION CORE
				Craft the Core at a Mythril Anvil using 12 Profound Iron Bars, 8 Spirit Jade Bars and 15 Spirit Stones. Place it on solid ground. The first cultivator who interacts with it becomes its Path owner and receives its training progress. Right-click while holding a Spirit Stone to insert it: each stone stores 250 Qi and repairs the Core, but grants no EXP. Right-click normally to open the Formation control panel. Its Formations tab controls active arrays; its Core Upgrade tab displays the next structural Stage and every changed statistic, including capacity, integrity, radius, repair speed, array slots, Relay limit and Tribulation absorption. Only the owner can change modes, power, contribution access or structural rank. Contribution access may allow only the owner, the owner's Terraria team, or everyone to insert Spirit Stones, while upgrades remain owner-only. The owner's Array Formation Path must already have reached the target rank, and every upgrade consumes Spirit Stones, Profound Iron Bars and Spirit Jade Bars. Tier breakthroughs additionally require a matching Beast Core; the final Tier consumes three Core Formation Beast Cores. Major Tier upgrades require confirmation before materials are consumed. Existing Cores retain their saved rank but never copy later Path advancements. Shift and Alt combinations remain optional shortcuts for experienced users. Two compact world bars appear above the Core and every linked Relay Flag: cyan represents shared Qi and green represents shared integrity. Empty dim bars identify an unlinked Flag.

				FORMATION TYPES
				Protection - Tier 0, 1 Qi/s. Grants +12 defense and 6% damage reduction, repels enemies and is the only type that intercepts Heavenly Tribulation lightning. Hostile creatures cannot naturally spawn anywhere inside the Core or Relay Flag territories, even when the boundary is outside the player's screen; harmless critters and friendly NPCs remain unaffected. Damaging projectiles and abilities created outside are destroyed when they strike its boundary and damage the Core's integrity. Projectiles created inside are marked as friendly to that territory and can leave without resistance.
				Spirit Gathering - Tier 1, 2 Qi/s. Increases meditation and passive Qi recovery by 50% for every cultivator inside.
				Suppression - Tier 2, 2 Qi/s. Slows ordinary enemies and applies Broken Armor throughout the territory; bosses resist most of the effect.
				Restoration - Tier 3, 3 Qi/s. Grants continuous life regeneration to cultivators inside.
				Array slots allow multiple types to operate from the same Core. Tier 0 has 1 slot, Tier 1 has 2, Tier 2 retains 2, Tier 3 has 3 and Tier 4 can run all 4 types together. Upkeep is additive: activating every type costs 8 Qi/s. At least one type must remain enabled. The Core seal and boundary particles show the currently selected type, while the status readout lists every active array. A Spirit Vein powers every enabled type without consuming stored Qi.

				FORMATION RELAY FLAGS
				A Core's own radius can never exceed 80 blocks. To expand farther, craft a Formation Relay Flag at a Mythril Anvil with 6 Profound Iron Bars, 4 Spirit Jade Bars and 5 Spirit Stones. A Relay can link with its center up to 40 blocks beyond the Core's current boundary, equal to the Core radius plus the Relay's 40-block territory. A maximum-radius Core can therefore reach a Relay 120 blocks away. This allows the new territory to begin outside the original Formation while remaining connected. Structural Tier controls the Relay limit: Tier 0 supports none, then Tier 1/2/3/4 support 1/2/4/6 Flags. Flags beyond the limit remain unpowered until the Core is upgraded or another eligible Core is available. A linked Flag consumes 1 Qi/s while its territory is empty and 2 Qi/s while a player or hostile creature is inside. It shares the Core's Qi and integrity. Right-click a Relay to open its status panel, showing its parent Core, connection distance, current upkeep, shared resources and local spiritual concentration. The Core owner selects one exclusive Relay specialization: the normal Core modes and the other specializations do not operate inside that Relay territory. Protection grants +24 defense and 12% damage reduction, stronger repulsion, 10% more Tribulation absorption and reduced barrier strain; Gathering raises meditation and passive recovery to 2.25x; Suppression applies a much stronger slow; Restoration grants +20 life regeneration. A specialization whose Core mode is disabled remains selected but provides no bonus. Projectiles created inside either the Core territory or one of its Flags can leave freely. If the Core deactivates, every linked Flag loses power.
				Selecting Normal Extension removes the specialization and makes every Core-enabled mode operate in the Relay territory at its standard strength.

				POWER AND TERRITORY
				An active Core pays the combined upkeep of every enabled array and persists with the world. Damaged integrity is then repaired automatically at a rate determined by structural Tier and Stage: every 10 integrity repaired consumes 1 additional Qi. Repair Qi is charged only while integrity is missing and is separate from array upkeep. If the stored reserve cannot pay the complete repair, the Core repairs as much as it can after paying upkeep. A Spirit Stone mine near the Core or any authorized Relay links through the same configurable radius and concentration calculation used by cultivators. Every node calculates its own local concentration and provides at most 5 Qi/s per level, from 5 Qi/s at Level 1 to 50 Qi/s at Level 10. This lets a Relay channel a distant mine into the shared network; multiple linked nodes add their individually capped production. Network output pays array upkeep first, automatic repair second, and stores only the remaining Qi. If its output is insufficient, the deficit is taken from stored Qi. An inactive Core has no upkeep and therefore continues charging its reserve from connected sources, up to capacity.

				During a Heavenly Tribulation, the Core directly intercepts lightning that hits a cultivator inside its territory. It initially absorbs 55% of each strike; Formation Tier and Stage can raise this to 80%. Tribulation lightning consumes much more integrity than ordinary attacks, with higher Realm Tribulations applying greater strain. A Core at zero integrity shatters, deactivates and leaves the remaining lightning damage to the cultivator. Qi Protection is applied afterward to whatever passes through the Formation.

				Relay Flags are the first territorial network component. Future updates can expand this system with permissions, specialized nodes and links between multiple Cores.
				'''
		}
	}
}
